{"id": "tea:taway-shenje:critique-qualifier", "source": "src:taway-shenje", "location": {"ref": "critique-qualifier"}, "paraphrase": "Tsongkhapa's addition of the qualifier 'inherently' or 'truly' to the object of negation is not found in Nāgārjuna and Candrakīrti, who negate arising, existence and the rest without qualification; by leaving conventional things unnegated at the level of ultimate analysis, that system clings to a subtle existence.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["dispute"], "teachers": ["tch:gorampa"], "disputes": ["dsp:object-of-negation-madhyamaka"], "notes": "Summary-level; recalled.", "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:taway-shenje:freedom-from-extremes", "source": "src:taway-shenje", "location": {"ref": "freedom-from-extremes"}, "paraphrase": "The ultimate is freedom from all elaborations — from the four extremes of existence, non-existence, both and neither; the negation of true existence alone is only a step, and clinging to emptiness as a mere negation is itself an extreme to be abandoned.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:gorampa"], "terms": ["trm:tropdral", "trm:catuskoti"], "concepts": ["cpt:freedom-from-elaborations"], "disputes": ["dsp:object-of-negation-madhyamaka"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:taway-shenje:three-views", "source": "src:taway-shenje", "location": {"ref": "three-views"}, "paraphrase": "In Tibet three views are held to be Madhyamaka: the Madhyamaka of the eternalist extreme (Dolpopa: the ultimate is empty of other but not of itself), the Madhyamaka of the nihilist extreme (Tsongkhapa: the ultimate is the mere negation of true existence), and the Madhyamaka free from extremes, which is the view of the Sakya and of Nāgārjuna.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["dispute", "ultimate"], "teachers": ["tch:gorampa"], "disputes": ["dsp:object-of-negation-madhyamaka", "dsp:rangtong-shentong"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:taway-shenje:ultimate-not-object", "source": "src:taway-shenje", "location": {"ref": "ultimate-not-object"}, "paraphrase": "The ultimate truth is not an object of knowledge in the ordinary sense: it is beyond the scope of mind and words; ultimate truth is 'known' only in the sense that, in meditative equipoise, subject and object are no longer divided.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ultimate", "dispute"], "teachers": ["tch:gorampa"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-the-ultimate-knowable"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U47-sakya-kadam-gelug"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
